---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';

const blogDisplay = site.blogUrl.replace('https://', '').replace('/', '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Magic Apps"
  description="What Magic Apps does with your data. Short version: the apps send nothing anywhere, and this site collects only an email address if you type one in."
  ogDescription="What Magic Apps does with your data. Short version: almost nothing."
  icon="suite.svg"
  current="privacy"
  permalink="privacy.html"
>
  <section class="wrap band" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h1 id="privacy-title">What happens to your data</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Short version: your mail and calendar data travels directly between your Mac and
        Google. This site collects no personal analytics, and the apps collect no usage telemetry.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        There is no analytics, tracking pixels, or third-party advertising on this site.
        It sets no cookies. Waitlist registration forms are embedded via EmailOctopus
        to collect email addresses with your explicit consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is served from Cloudflare's edge, which keeps its own request logs. Those
        are Cloudflare's, not ours, and we do not read them. See <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Cloudflare's privacy policy <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The apps themselves</h2>
      <p>
        Your credentials, emails, calendar events, contacts, and tasks travel exclusively
        and directly between your Mac and Google's official servers. We operate no
        intermediate servers, proxies, or relays that touch, inspect, or store your communications.
        We cannot read your mail or events, and we have no record of your accounts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything the apps store stays in your local user library on your Mac. The apps collect
        no behavioral analytics or usage telemetry. Automatic update checks connect to our release
        distribution server (updates.macmagic.app) to verify the latest release version without
        transmitting account information or personal data.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        If you are in the UK or the EU, you have the right to ask what we hold about you,
        to have it corrected or deleted, to withdraw consent, and to receive a copy. In
        practice there is only ever one thing to ask about, and unsubscribing already
        deletes it. The lawful basis for holding an address is your consent, given when you
        confirm it.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
      <p>
        {site.author} is the data controller. Ask anything, including to be deleted,
        via <a href={site.blogUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{blogDisplay} <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>.
      </p>

      <p class="small dim">Last updated {site.privacyUpdated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
